messages:
maria: Heads-up — I hit a weird auth/retry edge in the new Next.js starter with LangChain today. App bootstraps OK but some requests fail during SSR with 401s then succeed on retry.

devin: hm. Which starter? edge or ssr?

maria: edge (edge-runtime), samplekit from /examples/next-edge-llama. Repro steps: start with NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY set to ephemeral key from dev token endpoint, then hit /api/generate during cold start. Sometimes returns 401 from our hosted API, then client retries once and it goes through.

sam: can you paste logs? errors from fetch layer or runtime?

maria: logs show: "fetch failed: 401 Unauthorized" from our SDK wrapper, then our fetch wrapper retries once with a refreshed token and succeeds. snippet:

```
2026-03-19T14:22:01.123Z info auth: token expired, refreshing
2026-03-19T14:22:01.128Z warn api: request failed status=401 url=/v1/generate
2026-03-19T14:22:01.130Z info api: retrying request attempt=2
```

ellie: is the refresh happening in server code or in the client? Edge runtime has different lifetime for envs.

maria: server-side (edge function). We call /internal/issue-ephemeral which returns short-lived key, then pass to sdk.init({apiKey}) per request.

devin: that pattern is fragile because ephemeral token rotation + kernel warming means sometimes initial token not yet provisioned in our auth cache. SDK should do 1) deterministic backoff, 2) honor 401->refresh and non-idempotent safety. Do you have repro repo?

maria: pushed a tiny repro to gist: https://gist.github.com/maria/ephemeral-next-edge-repro

alex: quick idea: SDK could expose an init option for ephemeral token refresh hooks, e.g. {onAuthRefresh: async () => ...} so starter doesn't have to re-init per request. But that might conflict with per-request isolation for Private deployments.

sam: Another angle: add a tiny wrapper in the starter that caches the ephemeral key for 30s and serializes refreshes. That would reduce double-refresh storms during cold starts. Worth adding to starter to reduce onboarding friction.

maria: agreed. Also noticed parity gap: Python SDK has built-in auto-refresh for short-lived credentials; Node SDK currently relies on consumer to handle. That's surprising for users following our quickstart.

devin: noted. I'll add a backlog ticket to align Node parity: auto-refresh + optional hook. For now let's update the sample app to include the cache wrapper and mention it in README.

ellie: +1. Also we should add an automated small eval harness to the example app that runs a few quick prompt checks after startup to verify model responds and telemetry emits. That would catch silent auth/telemetry regressions before users start the app.

maria: prototype command for the harness: `npm run smoke && node ./scripts/eval-smoke.js` — eval-smoke hits 3 prompts and asserts no 401s and low latency.

sam: can you share the wrapper snippet? I can PR to the starter repo.

maria: sure, paste below:

```js
// ephemeral-cache.js
let cached = null;
let expiresAt = 0;
let inflight = null;

export async function getEphemeralKey(fetcher) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (cached && now < expiresAt) return cached;
  if (inflight) return inflight;
  inflight = (async () => {
    const res = await fetcher();
    cached = res.key;
    expiresAt = Date.now() + (res.ttl_ms || 30000);
    inflight = null;
    return cached;
  })();
  return inflight;
}
```

alex: that looks solid. We should mention in README that for edge starters using ephemeral tokens, prefer caching and serializing refreshes.

ci-bot: deploy-preview built for branch/devex/ephemeral-fix — smoke tests: 3/3 passed. :white_check_mark:

maria: thanks! can we also add a short note in devex docs about SDK parity and the known Node auth gap? It trips internal new hires too.

devin: will do. Adding ticket: RED-DEVEX-461. Owner: devin. ETA: next sprint.

ellie: final ask — add a tiny example eval prompt set (3 prompts) and an example failure message for users to triage "401 then success" pattern. That will help support.

maria: I'll open the starter PR with the wrapper, smoke harness, README note, and prompt set. Thanks all. :party_parrot:
